threads.body:
Both libraries support hosted web search, so per the contract they need a `server_tool_calling` scenario too, like Python `openai` has. Something like:

```js
// openai/scenarios/server_tool_calling.js
await client().responses.create({
  model: "gpt-4o-mini",
  instructions: "You are a helpful assistant.",
  input: "What is OpenTelemetry?",
  tools: [{ type: "web_search" }],
  max_output_tokens: 100,
  temperature: 0.5,
});
```

```js
// vercel-ai/scenarios/server_tool_calling.js
const openai = provider();
await generateText({
  ...request(),
  model: openai.responses("gpt-4o-mini"),
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "What is OpenTelemetry?" }],
  tools: { web_search: openai.tools.webSearch({}) },
});
```

